<title>UK: MTL plans to axe up to 1,200 jobs - paper.</title>
<headline>MTL plans to axe up to 1,200 jobs - paper.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>MTL Trust Holdings, the Liverpool based transport group which recently won the Regional Railways North East rail franchise under UK privatisation plans, is set to axe up to 1,200 jobs in the rail company, said the Financial Times on Thursday.</p>
<p>The report said MTL needed to shed 40 percent of the workforce at the RRNE franchise company in order to meet its financial projections to cut costs.</p>
<p>It takes over the passenger rail franchise next Sunday and has also warned it may need to cut 350 jobs at Merseyside Electrics, its other rail franchise.</p>
<p>The estimates for job cuts was made in the company's franchise bid documents which have been leaked. --London newsroom +44 171 5427717</p>
